  particular: no use to develop or train AI or voice models).

LiveKit Agents
  Parts of the voice agent are adapted from LiveKit Agents
  (https://github.com/livekit/agents and https://github.com/livekit/agents-js),
  Copyright LiveKit, Inc., licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (a copy is in
  licenses/Apache-2.0.txt):
  - apps/agent/src/collect/collectors.ts and apps/agent/src/collect/collect-task.ts
    are ported from LiveKit's Python ready-made tasks (GetPhoneNumberTask,
    GetNameTask, GetEmailTask, GetAddressTask); their prompts and checks are
    close to LiveKit's.
  - patches/@livekit__agents@*.patch changes the LiveKit Agents package itself.
  Linedesk changed these parts. The changes are under the MIT license.

LiveKit model weights
  The voice agent uses LiveKit Agents, which depends on the
  @livekit/local-inference package (version 0.3.1 at the time of writing).
  The native binary of that package contains model weights, among them
  LiveKit's end-of-turn model. So the weights are not in this repository's
  source, but they come with that npm package after `pnpm install` and are in
  the agent image. LiveKit's models are under LiveKit's own model license
  (MODEL_LICENSE in that package), which allows their use only together with
  LiveKit Agents. Linedesk turns local inference off by default
  (apps/agent/src/env.ts), but the package is still installed.

Holiday data
  The API uses the date-holidays package by commenthol and contributors
  (https://github.com/commenthol/date-holidays), with its date-holidays-parser
  package. Their code is under the ISC license. The holiday data in
  date-holidays (data/holidays.json and data/countries/*.yaml), mostly from
  Wikipedia articles, is under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike: the
  package declares CC-BY-SA-4.0 (package.json, LICENSE, holidays.json), while
  its README and the attribution list in its LICENSE file name CC BY-SA 3.0,
  the license of the Wikipedia text it was taken from. The attribution (the
  source articles) is in the package's LICENSE file. Linedesk does not include
  this data in the repository; it comes with the package.

